                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Good premise, but buggier than a $5 hotel room.\n\nFix the annoying menu flash, the wierd screen resize issue, the loss of mouse pointer after resize, and the recentering of the window at random times and then we can focus on the game rather the fustration of the UI.\n",
                        "timestamp_created": 1450251652,
                        "timestamp_updated": 1450251652,
                        "voted_up": true,
                        "votes_up": 35,
                        "votes_funny": 9,
                        "weighted_vote_score": 0.6910942792892456,
                        "comment_count": 7,
                        "steam_purchase": true,
                        "received_for_free": false,
                        "written_during_early_access": false,
                        "developer_response": "Hi there Arkady! Cheers for the review, your feedback is a big deal -- it means a lot that you dig the game despite the UI weirdness you're totally right about. Just wanted to let you know that we released an update yesterday (v0.82) that's improved on the silliness with the freaky menu bar, the recentering window, the vanishing mouse pointer, etc., and added in a much, much better fullscreen option when you maximize the game window (which is now the default on launch). Here's hoping you find Gigachess to be a much smoother experience when you fire it up next!",
                        "timestamp_dev_responded": 1450371538,
                        "primarily_steam_deck": false,
                        "refunded": false
                    }
